            {
                "question": "What German standards cover forged steel for pressure vessels?",
                "answer": "Primary standards: EN 13445 (Unfired Pressure Vessels \u2014 the European pressure vessel design standard, adopted in Germany as DIN EN 13445), PED 2014/68/EU (directive requiring CE marking for pressure equipment above threshold P\u00d7V), DIN EN 10273 (Hot-rolled weldable steel bars for pressure purposes \u2014 for flanges and nozzle forgings), and DIN EN 10028 parts 1\u20137 (Flat products in steel for pressure purposes). Our ASME SA-grade materials have full DIN EN equivalence documentation."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can you supply Siemens Energy gas turbine disk forgings?",
                "answer": "Yes. For Siemens Energy's SGT-800/H-class turbines: HP turbine disk forgings in IN706 or Waspaloy nickel superalloy (T 900\u00b0C HPT service), compressor disk blank forgings in Ti-6Al-4V (AMS 4928 equivalent, low-pressure stages), and combustion chamber casing forgings in Hastelloy X (AMS 5536 equivalent). EN 10204 3.2, 100% UT per EN 10228-1 (ultrasonic Class B), Siemens Energy supplier qualification documentation."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can you supply BOF trunnion ring forgings for Thyssenkrupp Duisburg?",
                "answer": "Yes. For Thyssenkrupp's Duisburg BOF converters (300-tonne steel converters, 30+ heats/day): trunnion ring forgings in 42CrMo4 Q+T (Rm \u2265900 MPa, Charpy at 0\u00b0C \u226547 J), OD 2,000\u20133,000mm, weight 8\u201315 tonnes per trunnion. EN 10204 3.1, 100% UT per EN 10228-3, hardness mapping at 8 radial positions. Also blast furnace trunnion forgings in 4340 Q+T. CIF Duisburg via Rotterdam + Rhine barge."
            },
            {
                "question": "What is the transit time from India to Germany?",
                "answer": "12\u201315 days CIF Hamburg or CIF Bremen from Mundra via Suez Canal + North Sea. Air freight Mumbai \u2192 Frankfurt (FRA) or Munich (MUC): 2\u20134 days via Dubai or direct charter. EU MFN import duty on forged steel from India: 2.7% for most HS codes. Rotterdam + Rhine barge to inland Germany: additional 3\u20135 days depending on destination (Duisburg, Cologne, Mannheim, Frankfurt)."
            }
