                "question": "Does Australia use ASME or AS/NZS pressure vessel standards?",
                "answer": "Both. Large Australian LNG and chemical plants (Woodside, Chevron Gorgon, Santos GLNG) predominantly use ASME Section VIII Div.1 as the pressure vessel design code (influenced by US EPC contractors like Bechtel, Worley, Fluor). Australian manufacturers and smaller projects use AS 1210 (Pressure Vessels \u2014 based on AS ME principles). For mining equipment (Rio Tinto, BHP, Fortescue): AS 1085 (mining specific) + ASME VIII for pressure vessels. We supply ASME CMTR-equivalent mill test reports, AS 1210 compliance statements, and EN 10204 3.1 simultaneously."
